+# Tasks: Log Redaction CLI
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-logredact-cli/`
+
+**Prerequisites**: [plan.md](./plan.md), [spec.md](./spec.md), [research.md](./research.md),
+[data-model.md](./data-model.md), [contracts/cli.md](./contracts/cli.md),
+[quickstart.md](./quickstart.md)
+
+**Tests**: Test tasks ARE included and are mandatory for this feature. Constitution principle III
+("Every Requirement Is Testable") requires each FR to map to a named pytest test, SC-004 requires
+100% FR coverage by tests that name the requirement, and SC-005 requires every failure mode to
+assert both the diagnostic and the exit status. Test ids below are taken verbatim from the
+requirement→test map in [quickstart.md](./quickstart.md#requirement--test-map-sc-004) — do not
+rename them, because that map is the coverage artifact SC-004 is checked against.
+
+**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story to enable independent implementation and
+testing of each story.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (US1, US2, US3, US4)
+- Include exact file paths in descriptions
+
+## Path Conventions
+
+Single project, `src/` layout, per [plan.md](./plan.md) "Project Structure". All paths are
+relative to the repository root.
