+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Redact a piped log stream (Priority: P1) 🎯 MVP
+
+**Goal**: Arbitrary text in on stdin, sanitised text out on stdout — emails → `[EMAIL]`, IPv4
+addresses → `[IP]`, Luhn-valid 13-19 digit cards (including their separators) → `[CARD]`, with
+every other byte reproduced exactly. This is the whole redaction engine plus the simplest CLI
+that exercises it.
+
+**Independent Test**: Pipe a log excerpt containing each kind of sensitive value on stdin with no
+file arguments; confirm stdout contains `[EMAIL]`, `[IP]`, and `[CARD]` in place of those values,
+all other characters on each line unchanged, line order preserved, stderr empty, exit status 0
+(quickstart.md Scenario 1).
+
+### Tests for User Story 1 ⚠️
+
+> **NOTE: Write these tests FIRST and confirm they FAIL (import error or assertion) before
+> implementing T014-T018.** T006-T009 all edit `tests/test_redact.py`, so they are sequential;
+> T010 is in a different file and can run in parallel with all of them.
+
+- [ ] T006 [US1] Add email tests to `tests/test_redact.py`: `test_fr007_email_replaced_with_placeholder`, `test_fr008_email_grammar_accepts_dots_plus_and_subdomains` (must recognise `jane.doe+test@mail.example.com`; grammar is "a local part of one or more characters drawn from letters, digits, and the characters `.`, `_`, `%`, `+`, and `-`, followed by `@`, followed by one or more dot-separated labels of letters, digits, and `-`, ending in a final label of at least two letters"), and `test_fr009_non_email_text_left_unchanged` (a bare `@`, `jane@localhost`, and a domain whose final label is fewer than two letters must all pass through unchanged)
+- [ ] T007 [US1] Add IPv4 tests to `tests/test_redact.py`: `test_fr010_ipv4_replaced_with_placeholder`, `test_fr011_ipv4_octet_range_boundaries` (exactly four dot-separated decimal numbers "each in the range 0 to 255 inclusive, written without a leading `+` or `-`" — assert `0.0.0.0` and `255.255.255.255` redact), `test_fr012_out_of_range_or_wrong_part_count_left_unchanged` (`999.1.1.1`, `256.1.1.1`, `1.2.3` unchanged), and `test_fr013_ipv4_digit_boundary_and_trailing_period` (`1.2.3.4.5` wholly unchanged — not `1.[IP]`; `connect to 192.168.0.10.` → `connect to [IP].`; also cover the derived leading-zero decision from research D-002: `007.0.0.1` redacts, `0255.1.1.1` does not)
+- [ ] T008 [US1] Add card tests to `tests/test_redact.py`: `test_fr014_card_replaced_including_separators` (`4111 1111 1111 1111` becomes one `[CARD]`, not four — the internal separators are consumed), `test_fr015_card_length_separator_shapes_and_luhn` ("a run of 13 to 19 digits, whose digit groups may optionally be separated by single space or single hyphen characters, and whose digits taken in order pass the Luhn checksum"; cover `4111-1111-1111-1111`, mixed `4111-1111 1111-1111`, and bare `4111111111111111`), and `test_fr016_luhn_failure_length_and_digit_adjacency_left_unchanged` (`1234567890123` Luhn-invalid 13 digits, `123456789012` 12 digits, `11111111111111111111` 20 digits, `4111  1111 1111 1111` double space, `4111,1111,1111,1111` comma, `2026-11-20 10:00:00` — all unchanged; plus `x4111111111111111` → `x[CARD]` and the D-005 case `123 4111111111111111` → `123 [CARD]`)
+- [ ] T009 [US1] Add fidelity, overlap, and counting tests to `tests/test_redact.py`: `test_fr005_line_count_and_order_unchanged` (no line added, dropped, reordered, merged, or split), `test_fr017_leftmost_match_wins_and_email_beats_ipv4` (`user@1.2.3.4` → `user@[IP]`; each character redacted at most once; plus the research D-004 overlap case `card 4111111111111111 10.0.0.7` → `card [CARD] [IP]`), `test_fr018_placeholders_not_reexamined` (literal `[CARD]`, `[IP]`, `[EMAIL]` already in the input pass through unchanged and are not double-counted), and `test_fr020_counts_occurrences_not_distinct_values` (the same address three times counts 3; absent kinds report `0`)
+- [ ] T010 [P] [US1] Add stdin CLI tests to `tests/test_cli.py` using the `run_cli` helper: `test_fr002_reads_stdin_when_no_file_given` (asserts stdout, empty stderr, and exit 0 for `user jane@example.com from 10.0.0.7` → `user [EMAIL] from [IP]\n`), `test_fr025_exit_zero_when_all_inputs_read`, and an empty-stdin case asserting empty stdout with exit 0
+
+### Implementation for User Story 1
+
+- [ ] T011 [US1] Add the three rule patterns and their placeholder literals to `src/logredact/redact.py` per data-model.md §3 and research D-001/D-002/D-003, each compiled once at import (R3.5) and never per line: email source `[A-Za-z0-9._%+\-]+@(?:[A-Za-z0-9\-]+\.)+[A-Za-z]{2,}`; `OCTET = r"(?:25[0-5]|2[0-4]\d|[01]?\d?\d)"` and `IPV4 = rf"(?<!\d)(?<!\d\.){OCTET}(?:\.{OCTET}){{3}}(?!\d)(?!\.\d)"` (the `(?<!\d\.)` lookbehind is derived and load-bearing — without it `1.2.3.4.5` yields `1.[IP]`); card candidate `CARD = re.compile(r"(?<!\d)(?:\d[ \-]?){12,18}\d(?!\d)")`. Placeholders are the fixed literals `[EMAIL]`, `[IP]`, `[CARD]` — not configurable (R3.1)
+- [ ] T012 [US1] Implement `luhn(digits: str) -> bool` in `src/logredact/redact.py` per data-model.md §3 and research D-006: precondition is that `digits` contains only `0-9`; walking right to left, double every second digit, subtract 9 when the doubled value exceeds 9, sum, and return whether the total is divisible by 10. Length MUST NOT be checked here — the 13-19 digit bound is the pattern's job (R3.6)
+- [ ] T013 [US1] Implement the combined email+IPv4 pass A in `src/logredact/redact.py` as one `re.sub` over a `(?P<email>…)|(?P<ip>…)` alternation with **email written first**, per research D-004 — Python's leftmost-first alternation semantics are the entire implementation of FR-017's "leftmost wins, email before IPv4" clause, and `re.sub` not rescanning replacement text is FR-018 for free (R3.8, R3.9). Count each branch's substitutions as it fires
+- [ ] T014 [US1] Implement card pass B in `src/logredact/redact.py` as a `while` loop over `CARD.search(text, pos)` on pass A's output, per research D-005: on `luhn(digits)` (digits = the match with spaces and hyphens stripped) emit `[CARD]` and set `pos = m.end()`; otherwise emit one character and set `pos = m.start() + 1` so a Luhn-failing window is left unchanged and the scan re-enters one character later rather than consuming it (R3.11). Do NOT use `re.sub` here and do NOT search shorter sub-windows at the same start position — the accepted residual limitation is stated in research D-005
+- [ ] T015 [US1] Assemble `redact_text(text: str) -> tuple[str, Counts]` in `src/logredact/redact.py` from T013 and T014, returning the redacted text plus the `Counts` for that text. It performs no I/O and may assume a decoded `str` (Constitution "Validation boundary"); it runs IPv4 before cards per R3.10
+- [ ] T016 [US1] Add the `SIGPIPE` and broken-pipe handling to `src/logredact/__main__.py` per research D-010: call `signal.signal(signal.SIGPIPE, signal.SIG_DFL)` at startup guarded by `hasattr(signal, "SIGPIPE")` so Windows is unaffected, and wrap the final flush in a narrow `except BrokenPipeError` (a specific anticipated exception, permitted by Constitution principle II — no bare `except`). Expected result: `| head -2` gives empty stderr and exit 141, the way `cat` behaves
+- [ ] T017 [US1] Implement the stdin path in `src/logredact/__main__.py`: wrap `sys.stdin.buffer` and `sys.stdout.buffer` in `io.TextIOWrapper` with `encoding="utf-8"`, `newline=""`, `errors="strict"` per research D-008 (UTF-8 forced explicitly on **both** ends so an inherited `C` locale cannot crash on non-ASCII passthrough; `newline=""` keeps each terminator attached so `\r\n` and a missing final newline survive), iterate one line at a time calling `redact_text`, write each result immediately (one line resident in memory, per R2.5), and exit 0. Also add the `redact_text`/`Counts` re-exports to `src/logredact/__init__.py` as named in plan.md
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 is independently functional — quickstart.md Scenario 1 passes end to
+end, and `pytest tests/test_redact.py` is green. This is the MVP.
