+## Dependencies & Execution Order
+
+### Phase Dependencies
+
+- **Setup (Phase 1)**: No dependencies — start immediately
+- **Foundational (Phase 2)**: Depends on Setup — BLOCKS all user stories
+- **User Story 1 (Phase 3)**: Depends on Foundational. No dependency on any other story
+- **User Story 2 (Phase 4)**: Depends on Foundational **and on US1's `redact_text`** — file
+  handling is a thin layer over the engine, as spec.md states in US2's "Why this priority"
+- **User Story 3 (Phase 5)**: Depends on Foundational and on US1 (needs `Counts` flowing out of
+  `redact_text`). Its `test_fr020_single_tally_across_all_files` test also needs US2's file mode
+- **User Story 4 (Phase 6)**: Depends on US2 (it only applies to the named-file mode US2
+  introduces) and, for its no-tally-on-failure assertion, on US3
+- **Polish (Phase 7)**: Depends on all four stories
+
+This feature's stories are genuinely layered rather than parallel: the spec itself orders them
+that way (US2 "the redaction engine from Story 1 is a prerequisite"; US4 "it only applies to the
+named-file mode introduced in Story 2"). Each story is still **independently testable** at its
+checkpoint, which is what the phase structure buys.
+
+### Within Each User Story
+
+- Tests are written first and MUST FAIL before the implementation tasks of that story
+- Patterns → `luhn()` → passes → `redact_text()` → CLI wiring
+- Tasks editing the same file are sequential and carry no `[P]`
+
+### File-Conflict Map (why most tasks are not `[P]`)
+
+| File | Tasks that edit it |
+|---|---|
+| `src/logredact/redact.py` | T004, T011, T012, T013, T014, T015 |
+| `src/logredact/__main__.py` | T016, T017, T019, T020, T022, T023, T025, T026 |
+| `tests/test_redact.py` | T006, T007, T008, T009 |
+| `tests/test_cli.py` | T010, T018, T021, T024, T029, T030 |
+| `tests/test_corpus.py` | T027, T028 |
+| `src/logredact/__init__.py` | T003, T017 |
+
+### Parallel Opportunities
+
+- **Phase 1**: T003 runs in parallel with T002
+- **Phase 2**: T005 (`tests/conftest.py`) runs in parallel with T004 (`redact.py`)
+- **Phase 3**: T010 (`test_cli.py`) runs in parallel with the whole T006→T009 chain
+  (`test_redact.py`); T016 can be written in parallel with T011-T015 only if a different person
+  owns `__main__.py`
+- **Phase 7**: T027 ∥ T029 (different files); T028 follows T027, T030 follows T029
